body:
I can reliably reproduce this as long as I select the same material in both scenes simultaneously (I bound `reload saved scene` to Ctrl+R to refresh)

This patch fixes the issue for me:
```diff
diff --git a/editor/inspector/editor_properties.cpp b/editor/inspector/editor_properties.cpp
index d30eb8cb50..c6980ae01d 100644
--- a/editor/inspector/editor_properties.cpp
+++ b/editor/inspector/editor_properties.cpp
@@ -3331,8 +3331,7 @@ void EditorPropertyResource::_sub_inspector_object_id_selected(int p_id) {
 void EditorPropertyResource::_open_editor_pressed() {
 	Ref<Resource> res = get_edited_property_value();
 	if (res.is_valid()) {
-		// May clear the editor so do it deferred.
-		callable_mp(EditorNode::get_singleton(), &EditorNode::edit_item).call_deferred(res.ptr(), this);
+		EditorNode::get_singleton()->edit_item(res.ptr(), this);
 	}
 }
 ```

The `call_deferred` was originally introduced by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/7f63b0e8cdc0ef2369d3b623c5943e2b6cd1b1ae#diff-7913bc42139883fd449446a10224599f6b3290824a625008c8071722a1ece02c
